      "id": "bug-038",
      "timestamp": "2026-05-26T00:00:00.000Z",
      "error_message": "Starting a single-AutoDrive-step workflow with no other active vehicles leaves the game with no working inputs — WorkflowManager dialog cannot be closed, no keys registered",
      "file": "src/gui/WMLeaderVehicleSelectDialog.lua, src/WorkflowManager.lua",
      "root_cause": "WMLeaderVehicleSelectDialog:onOpen() built the vehicle list and, when no other vehicles were active, called self:close() synchronously inside onOpen(). Closing a dialog mid-open (before g_gui finishes the open transition / input-context push) corrupts the FS25 GUI input-context stack, leaving no active context so no inputs are recognized. Log showed onOpen immediately followed by onClose.",
      "fix": "Extracted list-building into WMLeaderVehicleSelectDialog:buildVehicleList() (returns candidate count, safe to call before showing). WorkflowManager:showLeaderSelectDialog now calls buildVehicleList() first and, if it returns 0, invokes callback(nil) and returns WITHOUT g_gui:showDialog — so the dialog is never opened-then-closed. Removed the close-in-onOpen path.",
      "tags": [
        "gui",
        "input-context",
        "dialog",
        "leader-select",
        "lua",
        "fs25"
      ],
      "related_bugs": [],
      "occurrences": 1,
      "last_seen": "2026-05-26T00:00:00.000Z"
    },
